The 'codegen' folder contains scripts that automatically generate TypeScript files from C# source definitions and constants, ensuring synchronization between the game's DSL (Domain Specific Language) definitions and their TypeScript implementations. These generation scripts fit into the project workflow by automating the creation of attribute and data files that would otherwise need to be manually maintained, reducing errors and saving development time. The generated files are then used by the TypeScript codebase to provide type safety and access to game DSL data.
